# lowered from the probe now.json by the fixture lowering (private tooling)
# The lane runs `ds-formal-tests --fixture` on this and diffs against
# now.expected (scripts/formal/check_idris.py). The Idris model's temporal
# fragment: `now()` is lowered as the clock
# leaf `now`, the wall sample in nanoseconds since the epoch (LTIM.2.8.3,
# LTIM.2.1.1), against instants folded from `calendar.time` (LTIM.14.1); the
# wall sample travels in `wall` steps -- the wall half of every `advance`,
# after its tick, and each `wall_set` (NTST.3.1) -- written because a `where`
# reads `now()`. Two kinds: Ping (0, relation: v Int key), Fresh (1, relation:
# k Int key). The time map's unit is 1 s, the gcd of the four 1 s advances;
# the ticks are 0 (the `set`), 1, 2, 3 and 4; the wall steps are the advances'
# 1 s, 2 s, 3 s and 4 s and the `wall_set` back to 1 s before the third pump.
# Rule 0 `window` is the witnesses' window `(now() > 0 and now() < 2 s) or
# now() > 2 s`; rule 1 `at_one` is `now() == 1 s`; rule 2 `fresh` emits Fresh
# logical under `now() < 2 s`; rule 3 `gone` has an untimed `no Fresh` node;
# rule 4 `held` is `p.dwell >= 3 s`, scaled by 1000000000. At (1, 1) `window`,
# `at_one` and `fresh` fire and Fresh blocks `gone`; at (2, 2) the three
# matches end, Fresh is retracted by the cascade and `gone` fires; at (3, 1)
# the wall is back and the three reopen as new matches, Fresh is emitted again
# and `held` matures on the monotonic clock; at (4, 2) they shut again, Fresh
# is retracted, `gone` fires and `held` persists. The key is the code of one
# Int (8 * zigzag(n) + 2); payloads the empty tuple (1); no text is read, so no
# `string` records.
schema 0 relation Ping
schema 1 relation Fresh
alpha 0 0
alpha 1 1
rule 0 window
pattern 0 0 0
where 0 0 or and gt now lit i:0 lt now lit i:2000000000 gt now lit i:2000000000
log 0 0 0
rule 1 at_one
pattern 1 0 0
where 1 0 eq now lit i:1000000000
log 1 0 0
rule 2 fresh
pattern 2 0 0
where 2 0 lt now lit i:2000000000
emit 2 1 1000000000000000000002 1
rule 3 gone
pattern 3 0 0
pattern 3 1 1
log 3 0 0
rule 4 held
pattern 4 0 0
where 4 0 ge mul lit i:1000000000 dwell 0 lit i:3000000000
log 4 0 1 slot 0 key 0
step tick 0
step assert _0 0 1000000000000000000018 1
step tick 1
step wall 1000000000
step pump
step tick 2
step wall 2000000000
step pump
step tick 3
step wall 3000000000
step wall 1000000000
step pump
step tick 4
step wall 2000000000
step pump
